From 2131fa1cc1e2b62a398541d9842c500b2902a190 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:52:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mac HDR export: one colour path for every frame (owner bug
 2026-11-12, orange skin at the start and now and then)

Source frames without colour primaries were read as if already BT.2020, skipping the BT.709 to BT.2020 conversion. Now every
source frame is read with resolved tags (its own complete ones, else its track's, else BT.709 SDR), and every composed output
buffer is stamped BT.2020 / HLG / BT.2020 matrix before Core Image draws it. MuseCore EditV2.HDRColor holds the rule and the
SDR/HLG maths (4 tests); the Edit ops snapshot check exports an untagged skin-tone take with captions in SDR and HDR and compares
every frame's decoded skin patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
